  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. Each player is dealt 13 cards\n2. One card is turned face-up to determine the wild card (joker)\n3. The remaining cards form the stock pile\n4. Players take turns drawing a card (from stock or discard pile) and discarding one\n5. Players arrange cards into sets and sequences\n6. A valid declaration requires at least two sequences, one of which must be pure (no jokers)\n7. When a player has valid combinations, they declare by discarding to the 'show' slot\n8. The player reveals their cards, organized into sets and sequences\n9. If valid, other players count points for unmatched cards\n10. If invalid, the declarer pays a penalty",
    Player: "1. Each player is dealt 13 cards\n2. One card is turned face-up to determine the wild card (joker)\n3. The remaining cards form the stock pile\n4. Players take turns drawing a card (from stock or discard pile) and discarding one\n5. Players arrange cards into sets and sequences\n6. A valid declaration requires at least two sequences, one of which must be pure (no jokers)\n7. When a player has valid combinations, they declare by discarding to the 'show' slot\n8. The player reveals their cards, organized into sets and sequences\n9. If valid, other players count points for unmatched cards\n10. If invalid, the declarer pays a penalty",
    objective: 'Arrange all 13 cards into valid combinations of sets (three or four cards of the same rank) and sequences (three or more consecutive cards of the same suit). Declare first to win the hand.',
    gameplay: "1. Each player is dealt 13 cards\n2. One card is turned face-up to determine the wild card (joker)\n3. The remaining cards form the stock pile\n4. Players take turns drawing a card (from stock or discard pile) and discarding one\n5. Players arrange cards into sets and sequences\n6. A valid declaration requires at least two sequences, one of which must be pure (no jokers)\n7. When a player has valid combinations, they declare by discarding to the 'show' slot\n8. The player reveals their cards, organized into sets and sequences\n9. If valid, other players count points for unmatched cards\n10. If invalid, the declarer pays a penalty",
    keyRules: [
      'Must have at least two sequences to declare',
      'One sequence must be pure (no jokers)',
      "A pure sequence can use a joker only if it's the actual card of that rank",
      'Sets cannot have two cards of the same suit',
